{#
  The macros the Markdown header and footer write a conversation with,
  imported `with context` so `markdownUrl` gives a page of the site its `.md`.

  `named(person)` is a person as a link, or their name when they have no URL.
  `said(entry)` is a reply's byline: its author, its date linked to where it
  can be read, and where it came from when that was not the comment form.
  `reply(entry)` is a reply as a list item, its words and its own replies
  indented under it, or the placeholder for a hidden one.
#}
{% macro named(person) %}{{ ("[" + (person.label | escapeMarkdown) + "](" + (person.url | markdownUrl) + ")") if person.url else (person.label | escapeMarkdown) }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro said(entry) %}{{ named(entry.author) }}, {{ ("[" + (entry.published | date) + "](" + (entry.url | markdownUrl) + ")") if entry.url else (entry.published | date) }}{{ ", via webmention" if entry.source == "webmention" }}{{ ", via the fediverse" if entry.source == "activitypub" }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro reply(entry) %}
{% if entry.withheld %}
- This comment is no longer shown.
{% else %}
- {{ said(entry) }}
{% if entry.rsvp %}

  {{ entry.rsvp.label | escapeMarkdown }}
{% endif %}
{% if entry.text %}

  {{ entry.text | nest(2) }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% for child in entry.replies %}

  {{ reply(child) | trim | nest(2) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}
